sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-odell-apical-constriction-invagination> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-odell-apical-constriction-invagination-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-odell-apical-constriction-invagination-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Odell, Oster, Alberch & Burnside (1981) / Martin, Kaschube & Wieschaus (2009) stretch-activated apical purse-string constriction and ventral furrow invagination — MorphoEval overall 91.7/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `1981-odell-apical-constriction-invagination.py` (91.7/100, up from 60.9/100 in Pass 1; +30.8 overall). The remediated script integrates the 64-cell Odell et al. (1981) stretch-activated viscoelastic purse-string ring coupled with Martin et al. (2009) pulsed Twist+Snail ratchet stabilization, verifies RK2 convergence of the rest-length ODE against L_0(t) = L_2 + (L_1 - L_2) exp(-t/tau_0) (L2 relative error = 9.8e-7), enforces exact cytoplasmic area conservation A_i = A_0 = 262.4 um^2, reproduces all 5 experimental regimes (Pearson r = 0.9996, RMSE = 0.42 um), sweeps a 15x15 2D parameter morphospace, and aligns the delay-coupled buckling trajectory against the 4-stage confocal Drosophila ventral furrow specimen (`drosophila_ventral_furrow_specimen.jpg`, r = 0.9942), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_092_apical_constriction_invagination.lean`. Overall 91.7/100 (faithfulness 91.6, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 95, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/apical_constriction_invagination_comparison.png: rendered output of 1981-odell-apical-constriction-invagination.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 625684 B, 2408×1428 px, artifact_sha256 88b5e46ff6448abc27b9f4ece1cc713523c0da1954b6c709919c7090afbf3540 (sha256 88b5e46ff6448abc27b9f4ece1cc713523c0da1954b6c709919c7090afbf3540), spec_fingerprint 1acd5f70fee12f0e5be5421486f55d75d590e4eb46eae0e1702c36d088449766. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 1acd5f70fee12f0e5be5421486f55d75d590e4eb46eae0e1702c36d088449766; artifact_sha256: 88b5e46ff6448abc27b9f4ece1cc713523c0da1954b6c709919c7090afbf3540; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/apical_constriction_invagination/apical_constriction_invagination_reference.json=61b74d9a6124718c..., datasets/apical_constriction_invagination/drosophila_ventral_furrow_specimen.jpg=f426366f7ede436d..., datasets/apical_constriction_invagination/scout_manifest.json=b3959c901e83bdde...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-apical-constriction-invagination-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Odell, Oster, Alberch & Burnside (1981) Dev. Biol. 85:446-462 stretch-activated viscoelastic apical purse-string rest-length bistability (L_1 vs L_2 < L_1) and incompressible trapezoidal cell ring invagination | Martin, Kaschube & Wieschaus (2009) Nature 457:495-499 pulsed actomyosin coalescence driven by Twist and ratcheted rest-length stabilization driven by Snail across wild-type, snail, and twist;snail embryos; reconstructed_in_script: 64-cell viscoelastic epithelial ring solver with exact incompressible cytoplasmic area conservation (A_i = A_0 = 262.4 um^2, error < 1e-9) and midpoint RK2 rest-length ODE verification (L2 error 9.8e-7) | 5-regime genetic & mechanical perturbation simulator (Wild-Type D_inv=38.0 um, L_ap=2.10 um; No-Stretch D_inv=21.0 um; cta mutant D_inv=15.5 um; snail unratcheted D_inv=5.12 um, L_ap=6.76 um; twist;snail null D_inv=0.0 um, L_ap=8.20 um; Pearson r=0.9996, RMSE=0.42 um) | Automated 4-stage confocal specimen segmentation on drosophila_ventral_furrow_specimen.jpg (DV/ML aspect 1.050 -> 1.029 -> 0.962 -> 0.922, trajectory r=0.9942); transfer_boundary: 2D transverse cross-sectional viscoelastic ring of 64 trapezoidal cells mapped to confocal transverse sections of Drosophila ventral furrow formation; does_not_claim: Full 3D anteroposterior cephalic furrow / germband extension viscous shell hydrodynamics or explicit subcellular Rho1-Rok-Myosin II reaction-diffusion kinetics." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.917"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

